Needs codex-vm -board-mmio, which the default harness does not pass. The BCM2711 peripheral base is 0xFE000000, above the RAM ceiling and exactly where codex-vm puts its emulated Intel HDA BAR. Since 2026-07-13 the guest page tables map the device gigabyte, and -board-mmio backs the window with RAM -- shadowing the HDA and xHCI BARs, which is why it is opt-in and not on for the default battery. With it, this test passes (6). Run it from build/boards-test.ps1, which is where the nine board batteries live.
